<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">United States Military Government of the Philippine Islands</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1898–1902</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Military Government of the Philippine Islands was the American military administration of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a> from the capture of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> in August 1898. Under a series of military governors it fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-american-war">Philippine–American War</a> against the First Philippine Republic. Civil authority passed to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippine-commission">Philippine Commission</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-howard-taft">William Howard Taft</a>, who became civil governor in July 1901, and military government formally ended in 1902.</p></div>
